"Progression refinement (supersedes strict exclusivity): maps carry OVERLAPPING index windows along the progression — e.g. map 1 offers indexes 0-4, map 2 offers the first 10 except 2 of them (repeats with map 1 expected), and so on: each map ends up with a FEW unique cookies (the fresh top of its window) while most spread across many maps as duplicates. Validation relaxes to indexes < bitCount (overlap is the norm, not an error); mustSpawn/canSpawn counts still apply per map. UI requirement: a cookie whose bit the VIEWER already holds renders 'stinky' EVERYWHERE it appears — on the ground before pickup included — so nobody thinks they found a reward they cannot use."